---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<PageLayout meta={{ title: "Pencil: AI Ad Infrastructure & Data Layer — Kiran S Baliga" }}>
	<article class="pt-6 pb-16 sm:pt-8 sm:pb-20">
		<a
			class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 mb-8 dark:text-neutral-400"
			href="/#work"
		>
			&larr; Back to selected work
		</a>

		{/* Article Header */}
		<header class="mb-10">
			<span class="block font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
				Pencil &middot; Engineering case study
			</span>

			<h1 class="font-sans text-[34px] leading-[1.3] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-6">
				A more dependable foundation for AI-powered advertising.
			</h1>

			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300 max-w-2xl">
				At Pencil, I worked on the infrastructure behind the creative workflow: how tenant data is accessed, how permissions compose, and how an ad report becomes a PDF.
			</p>

			{/* Role & Context Box */}
			<div class="border-y border-[#deded8] my-8 py-5 dark:border-neutral-800">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-3">
					<div>
						<span class="block font-sans text-sm font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
							Associate Software Engineer
						</span>
						<span class="font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
							KeyValue Software Systems &middot; Client engagement: Pencil
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="sm:text-right">
						<span class="block font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 tabular-nums">
							Sep 2023&ndash;Feb 2026
						</span>
						<a
							class="font-sans text-sm text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 dark:text-[#f5f4f1]"
							href="https://trypencil.com"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							trypencil.com &nearr;
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
					Node.js &middot; Python &middot; Google Cloud SQL &middot; Custom ORM &middot; Puppeteer &middot; Docker
				</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		{/* Context */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				The context
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Pencil is a B2B AI ad platform for agencies working across Google, Meta, TikTok and LinkedIn. Underneath those workflows, data access and document exports had to remain predictable as tenant-specific requirements grew.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				The work wasn’t a wholesale rewrite. It was a series of changes to make the existing platform faster and safer to evolve: fewer expensive joins, consistent tenant boundaries, flexible custom fields and a rendering pipeline we could control.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* Tenant Boundaries */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				Put tenant boundaries in the data layer
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				I built a custom ORM / data-access layer across Node.js and Python, with automatic tenant scoping and soft-delete enforcement. These rules became infrastructure, rather than conditions every caller had to remember.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				We reduced costly joins around real read workloads. Metadata-driven custom fields allowed the model to vary by tenant, while fine-grained RBAC supported composable AND / OR permissions instead of a growing set of one-off checks.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Cloud SQL migrations were rolled out incrementally. I coordinated the migration and downtime with the lead, using tenant-level feature flags to control the transition rather than switching every customer at once.
			</p>

			<div class="border-l-2 border-[#262625] dark:border-[#f5f4f1] pl-5 py-2 my-6">
				<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
					The result: a 30% improvement in API response times. The lesson was to optimize for the queries the product actually makes, not an idealized model.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Document Rendering */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				Move document rendering out of the browser
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				Exporting an ad report was originally tied to the client session: React rendered the page, a client-side library walked the DOM, and the browser generated a PDF on the fly. That worked for a single user looking at a simple table. It didn’t work for high-resolution proofs, large datasets, or scheduled batch exports.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
				I rebuilt the export pipeline as a standalone service running headless Puppeteer in a containerized worker pool. Templates were isolated from the web app, and assets were pre-warmed so exports could scale independently of the interactive UI.
			</p>

			{/* Pipeline Comparison Card */}
			<div class="relative bg-[#f8f7f4] dark:bg-neutral-900 border border-[#deded8] dark:border-neutral-800 rounded p-6 sm:p-7 my-6">
				<div class="space-y-5">
					<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-2 sm:gap-4">
						<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 w-16 uppercase">BEFORE</span>
						<span class="font-sans text-[15px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
							Browser UI &rarr; react-to-pdf &rarr; Download
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="border-t border-[#deded8] dark:border-neutral-800"></div>
					<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-2 sm:gap-4">
						<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400 w-16 uppercase">AFTER</span>
						<div>
							<span class="font-sans text-[15px] font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] block">
								Export request &rarr; Sandboxed Puppeteer worker &rarr; PDF
							</span>
							<span class="font-sans text-xs text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
								Preloaded fonts + cache + print CSS
							</span>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="hidden sm:block absolute -right-3 -top-6 select-none">
					<span class="font-handwriting text-2xl text-[#EE2796] rotate-[-4deg] block">
						control the<br />whole render
					</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<p class="font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">
				Different boundaries, different measurements: rendering time is only one part of the complete export journey.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* What Changed / Metrics */}
		<section class="space-y-6 mb-12">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1]">
				What changed
			</h2>

			<div class="space-y-5">
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						65%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Reduction in PDF rendering processing time.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						~1.5 sec
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Click-to-PDF download time.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-4 dark:border-neutral-800">
					<span class="font-sans text-2xl font-medium text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] w-28 shrink-0">
						30&ndash;40%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300">
						Reduction in end-to-end export pipeline latency &mdash; a separate measure from rendering processing time.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* What I'd carry into the next system */}
		<section class="space-y-4 mb-14">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[23px] font-normal text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] mb-3">
				What I’d carry into the next system
			</h2>
			<ul class="space-y-3 font-sans text-[17px] leading-[1.65] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300 list-disc pl-5">
				<li>
					<strong class="text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] font-medium">Design around real reads.</strong> A cleaner abstraction is only useful if it serves the workloads people depend on.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] font-medium">Make the safe path the default.</strong> Tenant scoping and deletion rules should be embedded in the infrastructure, not scattered across application code.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] font-medium">Own the rendering environment.</strong> A document is an output with its own requirements; it shouldn’t be an accidental screenshot of the UI.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-[#262625] dark:text-[#f5f4f1] font-medium">Modernize incrementally.</strong> Migrations and tenant-level flags let us improve the system without treating every change as a big-bang replacement.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		{/* Next Case Study */}
		<div class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-8 dark:border-neutral-800">
			<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2">
				<span class="font-sans text-sm text-[#797974] dark:text-neutral-400">Next case study</span>
				<a
					class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 dark:text-[#f5f4f1]"
					href="/#work"
				>
					Siren &mdash; agent tools &amp; MCP &rarr;
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-[#444441] dark:text-neutral-300 mt-4">
				Working through a similar engineering problem? <a class="underline hover:text-accent" href="mailto:kiransbaliga@gmail.com">Let’s talk about it.</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</PageLayout>
